sks associated with them?","No understanding / knowledge"]},{"passageId":"P9","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":null,"cells":["Have you invested in Unit Trusts and General Investment Accounts within the last 5 years?","No"]},{"passageId":"P9","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":null,"cells":["Have you invested in stocks and shares within the last 5 years?","No"]},{"passageId":"P9","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":null,"cells":["Have you invested in Current Accounts, Savings/Deposit Accounts, Cash ISA, National Savings and Investments within the last 5 years?","Yes, by myself"]},{"passageId":"P10","source":"Risk profile report.md","category":"D","quote":"No additional notes were recorded","cells":null},{"passageId":"P7","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"You confirmed that you wish to increase your Risk rating to 5- Balanced investor, you are aware that this is higher than your agreed risk rating and are happy to take on this risk with your pension. You have confirmed that you are not reliant upon your pension funds and wish for them to have the best growth potential over a 10-year period and feel a balanced approach to this investment would achieve this goal. You are aware that your funds may go up as well as down, and the higher risk you take with your funds, potential there is for larger drops in value. As a Balanced investor, you do not see yourself as a particularly cautious person and have no strong positive or negative associations with the notion of taking risk. If you have some experience in investments and a degree of understanding of financial matters, then you may be suited to a Balanced approach to investing.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P7","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"John, you are aware that investment values can rise as well as fall, and although your experience is limited to your workplace pension arrangements, you unde